# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your key.

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Gemini. This is the only AI provider SafeShift uses: it drives the
# agent under test, the red-team attacker, and the judge.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Server-side only — it is read inside lib/gemini.ts, which is imported by
# API routes only and never reaches the browser bundle.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Overrides the Gemini model used for every AI role. Defaults to gemini-3.5-flash-lite.
# Two things to know before changing it:
#   - gemini-2.5-flash is retired for newly-issued keys and returns 404.
#   - one crash test costs a dozen-plus requests, and the newest models have a
#     free-tier allowance as low as 20 requests/day. Check quota before pinning.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# Maya Research TTS — powers the spoken read-back in the voice scenario
# composer and the "hear the call" playback. Voice is optional; everything
# else works without it. https://docs.mayaresearch.ai
# MAYA_API_KEY=
